      en: "Värnamo Museum, established in 1936, is located in a former school building from 1890. Its permanent exhibition focuses on the history of Värnamo and surrounding Småland, with artifacts from the Stone Age to modern times. The museum highlights the region's textile industry, which peaked in the mid-20th century, employing over 2,000 workers. Notable exhibits include a reconstructed 19th-century workshop and a collection of traditional Swedish folk costumes. The museum also hosts a research library with over 10,000 volumes on local history.",
